==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|coppeweb}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|cop|t1=spider|web}}. Compare {{cog|dum|kopwebbe}}, {{cog|nds-de|Kobbenwebbe}} {{i|Westphalian}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|cob|web|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-cobweb.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[spiderweb]], or the [[remain]]s of one, especially an [[asymmetrical]] one that is woven with an irregular pattern of threads.
# One of its [[filament]]s; [[gossamer]]
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Something thin and [[unsubstantial]], or flimsy and worthless; [[rubbish]].
#* Sir Philip Sidney
#*: The dust and '''cobwebs''' of that uncivil age.
# An [[intricate]] [[plot]] to [[catch]] the [[unwary]]
#* Cowper
#*: Entangled in the '''cobwebs''' of the schools.
# {{lb|en|internet|rare|slang}} A [[web page]] that either has not been [[update]]d for a long time, or that is rarely [[visit]]ed
# The {{vern|European spotted flycatcher}}, {{taxlink|Muscicapa striata|species|noshow=1|ver=161002}}.<!--Webster 1913-->

